.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt DMA_MAP 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dma_map_single ,
.Nm dma_unmap_single
.Nd map and unmap a single DMA buffer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/dma.h
.Ft dma_addr_t
.Fn dma_map_single "void *cpu_addr" "size_t size" "enum dma_data_direction dir"
.Ft void
.Fn dma_unmap_single "dma_addr_t dma_addr" "size_t size" "enum dma_data_direction dir"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions translate a kernel buffer into a device-visible DMA
address and retire that mapping when the transfer is complete.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dma_alloc_coherent 9
